{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1923 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0b92470e1d7aad20d1d55a98f9214953e9ae079fdfcc76a608121b5cdfc8f7fe" :edb/db-before-t 1922 :edb/db-after-t 1923 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535235 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:10:46.855Z" 13194139535235 true] [17592186100802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339019 13194139535235 true] [17592186100802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339022 13194139535235 true] [17592186100803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339012 13194139535235 true] [17592186100803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339026 13194139535235 true] [17592186339012 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339013 13194139535235 true] [17592186339012 1089 "q-15759" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339012 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535235 true] [17592186339012 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339012 1113 #uuid "27bea004-4b63-5df6-b1f8-256ce7d09483" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339012 1145 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=x \\\\ y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNow, using the definition of a tangent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡t}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=y$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.$" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339014 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339015 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339016 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339017 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339018 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1041 "selection" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339016 13194139535235 true] [17592186339013 1110 #uuid "48eb6605-a5a6-5deb-9bd1-c52985f6ec88" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339014 1034 "y=\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{2+{x}^{2}}}" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339014 1111 #uuid "e012e206-3735-52c5-a282-bf2808614912" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339015 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4}}" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339015 1111 #uuid "856326c3-7667-54fa-a934-161221b007ed" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339016 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339016 1111 #uuid "e800c784-13ae-5601-9c36-93a4a0f3cd63" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339017 1034 "y=\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339017 1111 #uuid "fc573f65-a24e-520c-8eed-2b957f1759f7" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339018 1034 "y=\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339018 1111 #uuid "d421e68e-e389-5822-acdd-369907b97f6b" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339019 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339020 13194139535235 true] [17592186339019 1089 "q-276277" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339019 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535235 true] [17592186339019 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t+1,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}+4,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535235 true] [17592186339019 1113 #uuid "992d1ab3-8ed0-513c-9be8-a224e42f96bd" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339019 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=t+1\\,⇒\\,t=x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=x-1$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(x-1)^{2}+4 \\\\ y & ={x}^{2}-2x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is \n$y={x}^{2}-2x+5.$" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339020 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339021 13194139535235 true] [17592186339020 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535235 true] [17592186339020 1041 "field-1" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339020 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339021 13194139535235 true] [17592186339020 1110 #uuid "394f49e8-fe69-5db4-b535-7ab3013652df" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339021 1034 "(x-1)^2+4" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339021 1111 #uuid "8e5208b2-72e0-53de-b598-4f8f6bd822e2" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339022 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339023 13194139535235 true] [17592186339022 1089 "q-321090" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339022 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535235 true] [17592186339022 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-9},\\,\\,\\,y=3{t}^{2},\\,t\\ge 3.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ge 0.$" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339022 1113 #uuid "9a6c0c76-c6e1-50d8-a750-17e2c1877457" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339022 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for ${t}^{2}:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-9}\\,⇒\\,{t}^{2}={x}^{2}+9\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${t}^{2}={x}^{2}+9$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=3({x}^{2}+9)=3{x}^{2}+27.\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=3{x}^{2}+27.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ge 3$ and $x=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-9},$ we must have $x\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is $y=3{x}^{2}+27,\\,x\\ge 0.$" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339023 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339024 13194139535235 true] [17592186339023 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339025 13194139535235 true] [17592186339023 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535235 true] [17592186339023 1041 "field-1" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339023 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339024 13194139535235 true] [17592186339023 1110 #uuid "b71634b4-798f-5272-8da0-3e322ce25d66" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339024 1034 "3x^2+27" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339024 1111 #uuid "be260f14-3c7a-5677-885c-0241dadd515e" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339025 1034 "3x^2-27" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339025 1111 #uuid "85c5029b-6042-5acf-b9c3-c3eef283ec26" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339026 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339027 13194139535235 true] [17592186339026 1089 "q-321318" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339026 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535235 true] [17592186339026 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535235 true] [17592186339026 1113 #uuid "f8042d0b-4861-581a-af53-dc262d902695" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339026 1145 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{6} \\\\ y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the double-angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{5}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{5} & =2{(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{5} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36})-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{5} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{36}-1 \\\\ y & =5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{18}-5.$" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339027 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339028 13194139535235 true] [17592186339027 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535235 true] [17592186339027 1041 "field-1" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339027 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339028 13194139535235 true] [17592186339027 1110 #uuid "dbb48a5f-dd43-5754-a144-f2da4c59a204" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339028 1034 "\\frac{5x^2}{18}-5" 13194139535235 true] [17592186339028 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535235 true] [17592186339028 1111 #uuid "021c6d5c-2559-569e-a7f5-d9c0a624fa15" 13194139535235 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-15759" 17592186339012 "q-15759/selection" 17592186339013 "q-15759/selection/4270ce471c4ce9a66e49f95400e71b650a68fd881f3969cdcab1d278c99ebfc9" 17592186339014 "q-15759/selection/a0655ef1cb3cc936f889072c81e02e2d29fcf42137bdee6df5a20a53010a2585" 17592186339015 "q-15759/selection/b7097d7d64bc4d3b801053218e61bc493bb43c63ff9a04e1f1d7b957fec48cc9" 17592186339016 "q-15759/selection/b73df3f09b027ea742edf89215b44685994301a2e18a051bd743bb7837911e5b" 17592186339017 "q-15759/selection/f2b4ff3f3e4ce9856a8818abe29a8959d98d6f33b9d5c0d4e651aa6a3756eb60" 17592186339018 "q-276277" 17592186339019 "q-276277/field-1" 17592186339020 "q-276277/field-1/2ba420e819b8617c139dd76f0e145400e6b8ead7237ab3bdf011bf6f4feb1ba3" 17592186339021 "q-321090" 17592186339022 "q-321090/field-1" 17592186339023 "q-321090/field-1/5cfce5771c82cd5618abcaa63685b8c1df11973263cf